WEBVTT

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.380
Yamato, I'll keep my promise.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.360
Promise?

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.740
That I'll beat you and have
audience with Polaris!

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.740
It seems you have no more
hesitation... Hibiki.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:25.910
Byakko!

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.660
Cerberus.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.300
Anger?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.470
What is this anger of yours?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.980
You've killed far too many people!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.960
That is your reason for
judging me? Pitiful.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.440
If someone hadn't done this,
no one would have survived.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.750
One as intelligent as you should
be able to fathom my reasoning.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.810
I know. I get what you're saying...

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.470
But there's no way I can accept it!

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.500
I can't let someone go free
if they would sacrifice

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.850
others because it "can't be helped"!

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.250
How sentimental.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.010
That's right. Because I'm human!

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.200
So I'm not human?

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.230
Good, Hibiki.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.240
You are now as powerful as me.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.990
That's why I can stop you!

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.240
Why do you think you
were granted such power?

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.880
Truly, it is an ability
you were born with.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.040
But think about it:

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.260
What is ability?

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:04.050
You and I, and the others
who lagged behind,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.150
were chosen by Polaris from the start.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.640
We're pawns.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:13.880
One could say our current situation
is God's contrivance...

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:19.360
But that God was not almighty,
but a broken system.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.690
Who shall remain?

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.360
It seems that alone
was left to humanity.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.140
I know not the criteria for selection.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.160
It is, after all, the
actions of a broken system.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.160
Even Alcor...

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.680
Even he was bound to fall
prey to the wheels of fate.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.350
Because the system is at fault?

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.130
Or he himself was broken?

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.130
There's no way to know that now.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.550
You knew that much?

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.510
It's conjecture.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.430
And observing God's
reasoning changes nothing.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:59.570
I shall survive, use Polaris's
power and rewrite the world.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.120
That is all!

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.410
Yamato. You would rewrite
all the lives...

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.490
all the existing emotions
of the previous world?

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.540
That's right.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.900
True, if you could remake everything,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.250
you might be able to
create a splendid world.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.510
It's the preferred evolution.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:31.260
But if it's forced on us,
it's not our world at all.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.060
The world that our friends...

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:41.190
that Daichi and the
others wanted to protect

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.940
was the world that we lived in!

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.320
Otherwise, we wouldn't have
suffered, have struggled,

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.530
have anguished so much!

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.480
To rewrite order,

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.930
to make the world we lived
in have never existed...

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:03.470
Yamato, isn't that the same
as voluntarily choosing death?

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.130
Voluntary... death?

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.630
That choice is far too sad.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.470
That's why you'll stop me?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.600
Yes.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.390
Hibiki... What is living?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.680
It's continuing to make choices.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.700
It's continuing to think.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.280
That's how the world
goes on into the future.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.560
Those continual, mistaken
choices have led

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.780
to this current world.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:40.390
Yes, but... That's the
world we've lived in.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.430
You're saying you'll change that,

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.630
but unless it's changed through
the wills of us all...

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:49.110
People will surely be even more unhappy.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.050
How naïve.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:56.050
But I've survived up till
today, and that's my will.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:57.680
Cerberus.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.370
Our world is like a terminal cancer.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.870
Saying you'll change things
through individual will

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.530
is the rambling of a peace-loving fool.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:17.910
Why don't you understand
it's too late for humanity?!

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.290
Even so, was this
something YOU had to do?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.180
That's right. If I hadn't done it...

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.560
If I hadn't taken control,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.310
no one would have been able
to survive up to this day.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.750
Such is the responsibility
of those born with power.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.680
Whether such is desired
or not is irrelevant.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:43.560
I didn't want this power.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.360
Yamato.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.900
This grave responsibility....

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.200
It's hardly difficult.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:59.990
Has no one lent you a helping hand?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.250
Hand?

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.040
Unnecessary. It has no meaning.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.690
It DOES have meaning!

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.000
Living alone is... It's sad, right?

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.280
You are weak.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:17.030
It's fine to be weak. It
lets us work together!

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.750
As a rule, humans are alone.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.010
If so...

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:26.600
If so, why did you come all
the way to Nagoya to help me?!

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.590
You were a pawn, needed for my plan.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.590
I gave you the battle
experiences to become such.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:35.510
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:41.100
Why did you get my dead face clip,
which should only have gone to my friends?!

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.650
A human with no heart shouldn't
be able to be a friend.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:51.110
"Friend"? What utter nonsense!

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.490
Yamato!

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.330
I have to do this.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.280
Yamato, that's enough.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.580
Hibiki.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:14.610
It's enough, right?

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.810
You don't have to use supernatural
powers and change things.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.500
My friend is trying
to do something wrong.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.660
I have to stop him. Just stop!

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.830
Let's fix this. Then...

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.420
let's be friends again.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.840
Friends?

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:39.070
That's right. No more fighting.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.960
We'll just be normal friends.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:44.930
Yamato?

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.350
You're interesting.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.770
You're a very strange person yourself.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:58.780
Perhaps I should have
looked for you sooner.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.240
Yamato, no!

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.220
I cannot stop now.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.150
If I were one who could
change his choices,

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.660
I wouldn't be standing here today.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.120
I shall preserve my dignity.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.420
If you say that I am a
friend then, Hibiki...

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.420
You will kill me.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.650
Stop it!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.840
There's no reason for us to fight!

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:22.680
Come!

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.010
Nebiros! Zao Gongeng!

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:34.020
You all do not fully utilize
the demon-summoning app.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.230
What's that?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.440
Demonic fusion.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:57.630
Satan.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.020
Byakko!

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.230
It's seems you've lost
the dragon's protection.

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.230
Even you couldn't stop me, eh?

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.490
Farewell, Hibiki.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.710
What's that?! That demon?

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:45.760
Daichi.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.850
A friend's demon has arrived.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:50.820
What does this mean?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.650
Nitta... Everyone!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.330
It can't be. It's impossible!

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:03.020
It's not impossible at all.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.740
Everyone was with me.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.400
How could demons of the dead arrive?

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:09.870
It's inconceivable!

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:12.980
Thank you.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:19.170
I'll be using your demons, everyone.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.180
Berserk! Lugh!

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.080
Lorelei! Jack Frost!

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:42.500
Zochoten! Purple Mirror!

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.370
Suzaku! Pallas Athena!

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.380
Arioch! Byakko!

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.630
The Tyrant, Loki. The Angel, Metatron!

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.260
Loki! Metatron!

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.190
What's that?

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:26.440
Lucifer!

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.950
Yamato!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.480
Hibiki!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.720
It can't be right

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:13.750
for one person to force
change on the world.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.180
I wish everyone

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:20.050
could've genuinely thought
about the future, like you.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:23.670
Yamato. That's enough.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.170
You don't have to shoulder
everything alone.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.530
To think...

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:31.910
You really would stop me.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:33.820
I promised, didn't I?

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.220
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.700
Polaris.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.230
My wish is...

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.520
Hibiki!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:24.940
Daichi.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.940
You waiting long? Sorry 'bout that.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:29.790
It's okay.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.700
Hibiki, you're goin' to college, right?

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.200
That's why you spend Sundays
taking practice tests.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:40.230
For now, I guess.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.500
I can't think of anything else to do.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.150
Sounds like you.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.710
Is it enough?

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:52.510
Daichi, if you get into college,
what will you do then?

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.240
Well, find somethin' I wanna do!

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:56.720
What do you want to do?

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.310
Goin' on dates, on trips...

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:04.590
And drives! I just got my license.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:05.700
You want to play around.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.700
Work is for losers.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:08.730
Really?

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.450
Well, it's like... I'm just so nervous!

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.950
I can't really do anything.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:19.200
Yeah, true.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.850
Still, things will work out somehow.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:25.940
Whoa. That's unusually
optimistic for you, Hibiki.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.920
Really?

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.590
Well, it's because you can study.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.670
You're not anxious at all, are you?

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.200
You have to try harder, Daichi.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.430
Wanna do another study session?

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.180
Test-taking just finished.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.180
Let's quit talking about
study for a while.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.080
Oh, that's right.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.250
There's something I wanted to show you.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.670
Well, wanna see?

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.500
What is it?

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.270
Lend me your phone. Hold on.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.230
Ta-daa!

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.560
"Nicaea"?

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.490
Yes, Nicaea!

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:02.330
It's a secret but popular
"dead face" site!

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.080
Dead face?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.510
It's a joke site that shows
a video telling you the

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.790
instant your friend dies.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.510
Is that so?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.780
Looks interesting.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.480
And then, the kicker is
so funny that... Huh?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.140
What?

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:24.680
There!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.370
That's Io Nitta from Class C!

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.900
Who's that? A friend?

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.870
No. But I sure wanna be her friend...

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.380
Looks like she's coming
home from a practice exam.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.640
She's cute, huh?

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.910
Yeah. Well, she's YOUR type.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.270
What the heck? You're
right, but still...

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.860
Say, are you coming back
from the practice exam, too?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.950
Dude, why are you callin' out to her?!

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.900
Well, you said you wanted
to be friends with her.

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.760
My heart isn't ready!

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.240
Daichi, your attention-grabber was okay.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.720
I ain't grabbin'!

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:05.720
I was startled when you
suddenly called out to me.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:08.960
Uh, we're not flirting or
anything. Not flirting.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.460
But YOU'RE flirting. Right, Daichi?

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.920
No, I'm not!

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.460
So long as it's as a friend...

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.570
Nitta, you're pretty friendly, huh?

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.920
I'm actually quite shy.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.560
Huh? You sure don't seem like it.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:29.370
Well, the two of you
don't seem threatening.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.060
Uh, is it okay to get happy?

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.470
What the heck, Hibiki?

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.900
Why're you so quiet?

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.380
Well, it just seems like fun.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.510
Huh? Hibiki, are you crying?

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.810
Why am I crying?

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.310
You okay? You feelin' bad?

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.840
Should I go buy some water?

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.440
It's nothing. Just, for some reason...

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:00.950
I'm happy.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:10.440
Oh, looks like a video has
already arrived from Nicaea.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.960
Huh? You're doing Nicaea?

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:13.960
You, too?

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.770
A friend invited me.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:18.710
It sure is popular, huh?

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:20.360
Let's see...

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.720
Hibiki, you're dead!

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.180
A tasteless site, isn't it?

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:28.180
Apologies for the wait.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:31.430
The train bound of Oshiage
will soon arrive at Track 2.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:35.380
Please stand back and wait
behind the yellow line.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.130
I...

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:52.630
What is it?

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.710
Sure enough, are you feelin' bad?

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:57.860
Oh. So that's it.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.920
Hey, Hibiki!

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:08.560
My wish... is to get a
chance to fix things.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:12.850
Sure enough, humans are
immature, like Yamato said.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:15.700
That's why we have to change.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.070
But a way

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:22.210
where one person has to shoulder
sadness can't be right.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:24.820
I...

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:27.710
I remember those seven days.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:32.120
I know how humanity is eliminated.

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:37.830
If I do nothing, humanity
will meet the same tragedy.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:42.460
That's why humans... have to change.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:49.480
Not by being forced to, but
slowly, through everyone's will.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.910
If we do that, surely... there's hope!

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.830
An interview? Beats me.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:00.090
Oh, the camera's this way?

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:04.240
My job's to get the gold medal!

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:09.950
Hinako! What do you
mean, you're leaving?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:13.700
I wanna see how popular
my dance can get.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.460
I'll think about takin' over
the house when I get back.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.610
Oh, excellent work.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.670
Good work.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:23.810
Mom!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:27.650
Hey! It's dangerous
to go out on your own.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:31.680
I told wait till I came
for you, didn't I?

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.010
I'm sorry.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:34.270
Jeez...

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.780
Well, let's go home.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:38.630
Yeah.

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.500
You're hungry, huh?

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.520
Yeah!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.400
Hey, Jungo!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.270
Why didn't you come see me?

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:02.500
It was the competition!

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.460
I had to work.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.330
You did well.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:11.390
Have some chawanmushi.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:16.600
My beloved is getting out
of the hospital today.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:19.380
Of course I'd come for her.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:20.710
I'm sorry.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:22.650
I thought you were someone suspicious.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.580
Man, that's rough!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:24.940
Joe?

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:27.860
You seem better.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:34.010
This is the log of the gang's
widespread dealings, huh?

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.120
That was a dangerous piece of work!

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:37.840
Thank you.

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:40.110
With this, we can corner the politician

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:41.750
s that have been sticking with them.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:46.450
Mr. Detective, you don't have to
act so reckless all on your own.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.100
It's my nature.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:51.760
I can't turn a blind eye
to those who misuse power.

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:54.700
If no one will do anything,
I have to do it myself.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:21:01.700
If someone start doing the right
thing, others will follow.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:07.730
Sakocchi?

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:18.520
What's with you?

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:19.330
Please let me in.

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:22.560
There's something I need to confirm!

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.330
Confirm what, exactly?

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.340
I have to see Yamato Hotsuin.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.220
Hotsuin? The heck?

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.590
It would be useless to explain.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:33.880
Please let me through.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:43.520
Yamato.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.970
Mr. Yamato? You know this man?

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:51.530
No. I have no friends.

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:12.260
Thank goodness. Yamato!

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:15.660
It's a good day.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:17.500
Sir?

00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:18.760
Don't worry.

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.570
It's just my state of mind.

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:38.010
I've watched over humanity
for a long time.

00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:41.400
It seems I'm no longer necessary.

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:46.000
I'm happy... and maybe sad as well.

00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:48.700
Humanity has shown its will.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:52.300
Living is... anxiety. And pain.

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:56.010
It's continuing to think,
continuing to choose.

00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:58.980
That's right, Hibiki.

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:04.400
I'm sure humanity can head
toward the right direction.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:10.200
Because humans can still cause miracles.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.390
We'll live.
